--dest-cpu=x64 is the only value whose gyp arch flag (-m64) the wasm64
target accepts -- ia32 emits -m32, which silently retargets clang to wasm32,
and arm64 emits -mbranch-protection=, a hard error. x64 in turn selects the
large-pages text-start marker, src/large_pages/node_text_start.S, which is
x86 assembly the assembler rejects on `.align 0x2000`: invalid alignment
value.

x64 also defines NODE_ENABLE_LARGE_CODE_PAGES, whose node_large_page.cc
references __start_lpstub, the start of a code section wasm-ld never
synthesizes: an unresolved GOT.mem import in node. Without the define,
`node --use-largepages` reports large pages unsupported, as node on arm64
Linux does.

